---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE, socialLinks, LEGAL_UPDATED, formatDate } from "../lib/site.mjs";

const social = socialLinks();
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What the Australian Election Tracker collects when you visit, how Google Analytics is used, and how candidate information is handled. How to request a correction."
>
  <div class="wrap wrap-narrow section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This site is a static public-interest reference. It has no accounts, logins or
      mailing lists. We use <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> to understand which
      pages people use so we can improve coverage of Australian election data.
      Candidate records contain only publicly available information about public
      candidacies.
    </p>

    <div class="notice" role="note">
      <strong>The short version.</strong> We measure aggregate traffic with Google
      Analytics so the site can stay useful as a go-to election data resource. We do
      not sell your data, run ads on this site, or maintain user accounts. If you email
      us, we have your email. If you post a GitHub issue, that's public.
    </div>

    <h2 id="analytics">Analytics (Google Analytics 4)</h2>
    <p>
      When you load a page, this site runs Google’s gtag.js script (Measurement ID{" "}
      <code>{SITE.gaMeasurementId}</code>). Google may set or read cookies and process
      technical details such as the page URL, approximate location, device/browser
      type, and referring site. Google acts as a processor for this measurement data
      under its own terms and privacy policy.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Why:</strong> to see which pages and data people use, fix weak spots,
        and improve the tracker as a national election resource.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What we do with it:</strong> aggregate reports only (page views, traffic
        sources, popular districts/regions). We do not use Analytics to identify you
        personally or to target advertising on this site.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What we do not run:</strong> advertising networks, session recording,
        heatmaps, or marketing pixels for third-party ad platforms.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">
      Google’s policies:{" "}
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="nofollow noopener"
        >Google Privacy Policy</a
      >{" "}
      and{" "}
      <a
        href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/6004245"
        rel="nofollow noopener">Google Analytics data practices</a
      >. You can also use browser controls, extensions, or Google’s tools that limit
      Analytics measurement.
    </p>

    <h2 id="not-collected">What we do not collect for our own systems</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No user accounts, logins, newsletters or mailing lists.</li>
      <li>No advertising networks or third-party marketing pixels on this site.</li>
      <li>No session recording or heatmaps.</li>
      <li>
        No fingerprinting beyond what Google Analytics may use for measurement; the
        site itself does not implement custom fingerprinting.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="processed">What is processed when you visit</h2>
    <p>
      The site is delivered by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare's servers
      process the technical details of each request — including your IP address, the
      time, the page requested and your browser's user-agent string — in order to serve
      the page and to protect against attacks and abuse. This is standard infrastructure
      logging.
    </p>
    <p>
      Separately, the Google Analytics tag described above sends measurement data to
      Google when the page loads (subject to your browser and any blocking tools).
    </p>
    <p>
      Cloudflare also enables Network Error Logging on the sites it serves. If your
      browser fails to load a page, it may send a technical error report to Cloudflare's
      reporting endpoint. Successful requests are not reported.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Cloudflare acts as our hosting provider. See
      <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="nofollow noopener">
        Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="you-contact">If you contact us</h2>
    <p>
      Email sent to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> reaches a private
      mailbox. We keep correspondence for as long as needed to deal with the matter and
      to keep a record of corrections. We do not add you to any list, and we do not pass
      your details to anyone else.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you raise a correction through <a href={SITE.issues}>GitHub Issues</a>, be aware
      that issues are <strong>public</strong> and governed by GitHub's own terms and
      privacy policy. If your request involves anything you would rather not publish,
      email instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      We never publish the identity or contact details of anyone who submits information
      to us.
    </p>

    <h2 id="social">Our social accounts</h2>
    <p>
      The project maintains only the accounts listed below (Election Tracker brand).
      Personal or unrelated channels are not part of this site. See the repository
      document <code>docs/SOCIAL.md</code> for the brand split.
    </p>
    <ul>
      {
        social.map((s) => (
          <li>
            <a href={s.url} rel="nofollow noopener">
              {s.label}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you interact with those platforms, the platform collects information about you
      under its own policies, which we neither control nor receive in bulk. This website
      does not load like buttons or advertising pixels. Optional <strong>click-to-load</strong>
      YouTube explainers appear on some pages (for example voting and Assembly): a poster
      image and play control are served from this site first; the YouTube player and related
      network requests only load <strong>after you press play</strong>. You can always open
      the same videos on our{" "}
      <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" href="https://www.youtube.com/@electiontrackerau" rel="noopener"
        >YouTube channel</a
      >{" "}instead.
    </p>

    <h2 id="candidates">Information about candidates and members</h2>
    <p>
      This site records information about people acting in a public political capacity:
      candidates who have publicly announced or been endorsed, and sitting members of
      parliament. Every record is drawn from a published, cited source.
    </p>
    <p>We deliberately limit what is recorded:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>What we publish:</strong> name, the party and seat associated with the
        candidacy, its status, the dates of any change, the sources supporting each, and
        optionally a short public occupation or background line when already public in a
        campaign or political context.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What we never publish:</strong> home addresses, personal contact details,
        family or relationship details, sex/gender as a data field, children, employment
        that is not public in a political context, or any personal information the person
        has not themselves made public in the context of standing for office.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What we never record at all:</strong> rumour, speculation or unverified
        allegations.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Full detail is in the <a href="/methodology">methodology</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="corrections">Corrections, and asking us to remove something</h2>
    <p>
      If a record about you is wrong, out of date, or should not be there, tell us and we
      will deal with it promptly. Requests concerning living people are prioritised above
      all other work on this project.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because the dataset is a public Git repository, corrections are made by adding a
      new entry rather than silently erasing history — the correction and its reason
      remain visible. If you believe information should be removed entirely rather than
      corrected, say so and explain why, and we will consider it on the merits.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may also ask what information we hold about you.
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="handling">How we handle information generally</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to handle personal information consistently with the Australian Privacy
      Principles in the <i>Privacy Act 1988</i> (Cth): collect only what is needed, keep
      it accurate, keep it secure, and correct it when asked. No credentials, private
      correspondence or unpublished submissions are ever committed to the public
      repository.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you are unhappy with how we have handled a privacy matter, contact us first. If
      you remain dissatisfied, you may complain to the
      <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/" rel="nofollow noopener">
        Office of the Australian Information Commissioner</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a public-interest reference work not directed at children. We do not
      knowingly seek information from children. Analytics measurement may still run for
      any visitor who loads a page.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes materially, the date below changes with it. Because the site
      is published from a public repository, every past version of this page and the
      exact date it changed can be inspected in the
      <a href={SITE.repo}>commit history</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="updated muted">Last reviewed {formatDate(LEGAL_UPDATED)}.</p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  h2 {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }
  ul strong {
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .notice {
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }
  .updated {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
</style>
